 "notes": [
  "Fincentric divestiture closed August 15, 2024 (gain on disposition $21M in MI). PrimeOne (MI) held for sale at September 30, 2024 (BS assets 38, liabilities 7). ES segment printed with zero.",
  "IS \"(Gain) loss on dispositions, net\" printed (21) -> gain_disp +21. \"Other loss (income), net\" printed 2 (loss) -> oth_inc -2. Segment-table total expenses 2,141 = IS expenses 2,173 - gain 21 - equity income 11.",
  "Ratings \"statutorily required bonus accrual adjustment\" $6M ($5M after-tax), cat OTHER.",
  "CORP acquisition-related costs $2M pre-tax with $3M after-tax (as printed).",
  "TAX items (footnote h): \"tax reclass of $3 million associated with a disposition\" and \"tax expense of $1 million due to annualized effective tax rate differences for GAAP\". The release does not state the direction of the $3M reclass; recorded as +3 (add-back), the direction consistent with the printed totals (pre-tax items incl. interest 19, tax-line adjustment (6), after-tax aggregate 25). With it, item after-tax sum 23 vs printed aggregate 25 (rounding across items).",
  "ngaap.items_total_pre = operating-level \"Non-GAAP adjustments\" (25); interest adjustment (premium amortization benefit, footnote g) printed separately as 6 (adjusted interest 78 vs GAAP 72). 971 + 25 + 215 = 1,211 vs printed 1,210 (rounding).",
  "Segment rounding: MI items -21+10 = -11 vs printed -10; CI 4+2 = 6 vs printed 7; Corporate 16+2+1 = 19 vs printed 20; Corporate 73-20-1 = 52 vs adjusted 53.",
  "Non-GAAP adjusted tax line: non-GAAP adjustments (6), deal-related amortization 70. adj_oth_inc = other loss 2 (no adjustment) -> -2.",
  "cfpub: capex and nci_dist positive outflows; three-month FCF in fcf_pub_q / adj_fcf_pub_q.",
  "Guidance raised: Exhibit 8 bridge: deal amortization 2.85, IHS Markit merger costs 0.25, premium amortization benefit (0.10), restructuring 0.13, tax rate and other 0.02.",
  "No organic/constant-currency table."
 ],
